From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0792: the shader and pipeline storage is flushed before the hard exit (IGraphicsSystem::FlushShaderStorage, called by ReXApp::OnClosing)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (pipeline-cache diagnosis of 2026-11-27, scratch/pipeline-cache/DIAGNOSIS.md, section 3.5)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: ReXApp::OnClosing ends the process with std::_Exit, which runs no destructors and does not flush stdio, and the storage's
  writer thread dropped what was still queued when told to shut down. Defensive (the runs show no loss: created - transfer ==
  appended in all of them): IGraphicsSystem::FlushShaderStorage(timeout_ms) (default no-op) -> GraphicsSystem ->
  D3D12CommandProcessor -> PipelineCache::FlushShaderStorage, called before _Exit with a 500 ms bound and no wait on the command
  processor thread; the writer thread tracks when it is idle, writes what is queued before returning on shutdown, and an exit line
  '[pipeline-storage] at exit: ...' reports what this run appended. No cvar.
  Validated 2026-11-27 (scratch run x-exit, window closed 25 s after start with CloseMainWindow): 'Window closing, shutting down...' ->
  '[pipeline-storage] at exit: 0 descriptions appended ... queues written and files flushed in 0 ms' -> 'Title terminated; hard-exiting
  process.', the process gone 316 ms after the close, exit code 0. tools/run_game.py kills the game, so its runs never reach this
  path; a cold-cache close in the middle of a burst (loss test, DIAGNOSIS test 4) was not run.
Bucket: REDO

0792-storage-flush-at-exit.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, T0/T2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
@@ -143,6 +143,8 @@
     (void)shutdown;
     return {};
   }
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0792): IGraphicsSystem::FlushShaderStorage. Any thread.
+  virtual void FlushShaderStorage(uint32_t timeout_ms) { (void)timeout_ms; }
   virtual void InitializeShaderStorage(const std::filesystem::path& cache_root, uint32_t title_id,
                                        bool blocking);
 
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
